@startuml hitl-clarification-flow
' Human-in-the-loop clarification (ADR-032): the agent policy asks the user
' ONE question when the goal is ambiguous; the job pauses in awaiting_input
' (never a blocked worker), the answer re-dispatches it with the clarification.
' Builds on the agentic loop + live journal (ADR-030) and self-critique (ADR-031).

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor User
box "Browser"
  participant "Vue SPA\n(SearchDetailView)" as Front
end box
box "Backend"
  participant "Rust API\n(Axum)" as API
  database "PostgreSQL\n(research_jobs, agent_steps)" as DB
end box
box "Agent"
  participant "FastAPI\n(/tasks)" as FastAPI
  participant "Celery worker\n(agentic loop)" as Worker
end box

== Launch (agent mode, ambiguous goal) ==
User -> Front : goal: "jaguar" — Run the agent
Front -> API : POST /api/searches\n{keyword: "jaguar", mode: "agent"}
API -> DB : INSERT job (status=pending)
API -> FastAPI : POST /tasks {job_id, keyword,\nmode: "agent", clarification: null}
FastAPI -> Worker : Celery enqueue
API --> Front : 202 {job_id}
Front -> API : GET /api/searches/{id}/events  «SSE, ADR-026»

== The policy asks instead of guessing ==
Worker -> API : POST /internal/jobs/{id}/started
API -> DB : status = running
Worker -> Worker : policy.decide(goal, steps, hits)\n-> ask("The animal or the car?")
note right of Worker
  LLM policy (ADR-030). It may ask only if
  no clarification is present yet — the loop
  degrades a repeated ask to finish
  (one question per job, cost guard).
end note
Worker -> API : POST /internal/jobs/{id}/question\n{question}  «ClarificationRequester port»
API -> DB : status = awaiting_input\nquestion stored
Worker -> Worker : task ends (return)\n«a worker never blocks on a human»

note over API, DB
  The reaper (ADR-016) ignores awaiting_input:
  the job is paused on the user, not stuck.
end note

== The user answers ==
API --> Front : SSE update {status: awaiting_input, question}
Front -> User : 🙋 "The agent asks: The animal or the car?"\n+ answer form
User -> Front : "the car" — Answer
Front -> API : POST /api/searches/{id}/answer\n{answer: "the car"}  (JWT, owner only)
API -> DB : answer stored, status = pending\nDELETE agent_steps  «fresh journal (replace semantics)»
API -> FastAPI : POST /tasks {job_id, keyword,\nmode: "agent", clarification: "the car"}  «re-dispatch»
FastAPI -> Worker : Celery enqueue
API --> Front : 204
note right of API
  409 if the job is not awaiting_input
  (double answer, late submit).
end note

== The loop resumes with the clarification ==
Worker -> API : POST /internal/jobs/{id}/started
Worker -> Worker : goal = keyword +\n(user clarification: "the car")\n-> policy searches, refines, finishes\n-> self-critique (ADR-031)
Worker -> API : POST /internal/jobs/{id}/steps  (×N)\n«search, finish, critique»
API --> Front : SSE updates — the journal fills in live
Worker -> API : POST /internal/jobs/{id}/results
API -> DB : results stored, status = completed
API --> Front : SSE update {status: completed} — stream closes
Front -> User : Q&A recap + decision journal + timeline

@enduml
